' First simple example of infinite bobs

' Let's open 8 screens of 1 bitplanes in 320x256 
' It costs 8*(320*256/8) = 8 * 10240 = 80 KB of chip memory  
For I=0 To 7
   Screen Open I,320,256,4,Lowres
   Palette $0,$EEE
   Paper 0 : Cls : Flash Off : Curs Off : Hide 
Next 
Wait Vbl 

' The idea is to build cyclic conitnuous images  
'
' With this first simple example, we will draw NDB falling squares 

' Init of the stars
NDB=7
Dim X(NDB),Y(NDB),SPEED(NDB)
For I=0 To NDB
   X(I)=32+Rnd(256)
   Y(I)=-16
   SPEED(I)=2+(I mod 3)
Next 

' A first square will fall during 8 frames, one frame per screen 
' Then we will reset to the first screen but will continue to draw 
' the falling square   
' When the square reaches the end of the screen, the next square is
' drawn from the top 
' The final render can be built in a more esthetic way of course 

S=-1 : Rem index of the current screen

Ink 1
For I=0 To NDB
For J=0 To 255+16 Step SPEED(I)
   Add S,1,0 To 7
   Screen S
   Box X(I),Y(I) To X(I)+7*(SPEED(I)-1),Y(I)+7*(SPEED(I)-1)
   Add Y(I),SPEED(I)
Next 
Next 

' Let's play the animation 
Do 
   Add S,1,0 To 7
   Screen To Front S
   Wait Vbl 
Loop 
